[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: An open decision is how a question exists before it has an answer

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-OPEN-IS-THE-QUESTION
TITLE: An open decision is how a question exists before it has an answer
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: Real use shows a question that cannot be phrased as a decision, or shows contention living somewhere an open decision cannot express.
STATEMENT: >>>
A DECISION carries an `open` state, and that state IS the question. A question
posed but not answered is a decision node at STATUS open; answering it is a
transition to accepted or rejected.

There is therefore no separate node type for a question, an issue or an open
point, and no need for one. The degrees of freedom in a body of work are the
count of open decisions in its closure, which is a query rather than a field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A layer-zero grammar sketch on this branch dropped the open state, running proposed to accepted, which presumes an answer already exists and leaves a posed question with nowhere to live. Restoring it costs one word in a list and removes the argument for a question node type entirely.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
FLAGGED FOR RE-EVALUATION under real use, at the operator's request 2026-08-28: the concern is that it is not yet clear where CONTENTION lives in this model -- an open decision holds the question, but what holds two parties disagreeing about it is unproven. Revisit when the graph has been used in anger rather than authored.
<<<
